Note:- Key Learning

PV represents storage prepared for LVM.
VG acts as a storage pool.
LV provides flexible logical storage from the VG.
Filesystems can be created on logical volumes.
LVM allows logical volumes to be extended when free space is available.
Shrinking requires the filesystem to be reduced before reducing the LV.
LVM snapshots provide a point-in-time view of an LV.
pvs, vgs, and lvs are useful commands for monitoring LVM.
